{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Certain AsciiDoc document attributes provide metadata to the Antora page (for use in the UI template) or control how Antora processes the page. We refer to these as "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page attributes"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". There are three types of page attributes: custom, predefined, and intrinsic. This page explains the purpose of each type of page attribute, how they’re defined, and how they can be accessed from the UI template using the UI model."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Page attributes are all about providing metadata, whether that metadata is for Antora itself, for the UI template, for the user, or for a search index. By defining page attributes, you can store additional information about the page, which can then be accessed and used throughout the site."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A page attribute is defined just like any other AsciiDoc document attribute, typically using an attribute entry in the document header. Where a page attribute differs is that the name of the attribute must begin with "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-category"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). The presence of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " prefix allows Antora to identify it as a page attribute."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you’re wondering whether you need to add the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " prefix, ask yourself if you need to access the attribute from the UI template. If the answer is yes, then you need the prefix. Otherwise, the prefix is not required."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "tip"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s an example of page that defines two page attributes:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= Page Title\n:page-category: DevOps\n:page-edition: Enterprise\n\nMain content."
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " prefix is meant to provide a hint to both Antora and the author as to which attributes comprise the metadata for the page. By standardizing on the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " prefix, Antora is able to isolate page attributes from the numerous built-in and intrinsic attributes in AsciiDoc or defined by the AsciiDoc processor. The prefix also isolates the page attributes from internal attributes used to store reusable content within the page or site (aka custom content attributes)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "purpose-and-anatomy",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Purpose and anatomy"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To define a page attribute, you add an attribute entry to the page header and start the name with "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". It’s important to define the attribute entry in the header. Otherwise, the page attribute will not be found."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s an example of an "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "attribute entry"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "define-and-modify-attributes.html#attribute-entry"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " that defines a page attribute:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= Page Title\n:page-name-goes-here: value goes here"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The name of this page attribute is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "name-goes-here"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " prefix plus the custom name, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "name-goes-here"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). Its value is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "value goes here"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The name of the page attribute must adhere to the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "naming rules"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "define-and-modify-attributes.html#naming-rules"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " for a document attribute. The value can be left blank or it can be a string value. If the value is not blank, it must be offset from the closing colon ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ":"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") by at least one space."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Since page attributes are just special AsciiDoc document attributes, they can also be defined "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "site-wide"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "playbook:asciidoc-attributes.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in the Antora playbook or "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "per component version"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "ROOT:component-attributes.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in the component version descriptor."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "tip"
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "If you want to make information in an existing document attribute available as a page attribute, you must promote that attribute to a page attribute. You can promote a document attribute to a page attribute using an attribute reference."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "For example, let’s say you have the attribute "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "product-name"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " defined on the page or site. You can promote it to a page attribute using the following attribute entry:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "= Page Title\n:product-name: Name of My Product\n:page-product-name: {product-name}"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "asciidoc",
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The attribute reference is resolved immediately, so the page attribute named "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "page-product-name"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " now shares the same value as the document attribute named "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "product-name"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "promote-a-non-page-attribute",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Promote a non-page attribute"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "custom-attribute",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Define a custom page attribute"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Some page attributes receive special treatment in Antora. These page attributes have reserved names, but accept user-defined values for communicating information about the page to Antora. Examples include "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-aliases"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-layout"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-partial"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-aliases"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute allows you to configure alternate resource IDs for the current page. For example, to claim the old name of a page, you’d use:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= Page Title\n:page-aliases: old-page-name.adoc"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Unlike custom page attributes, the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-aliases"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute requires the value to conform to a specific syntax (i.e., a comma-separated list of resource IDs). See "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page aliases"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "page-aliases.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to learn about the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-aliases"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute and how it can be used to preserve references to a renamed, moved, or deleted page."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-layout"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute allows you to specify which UI template to apply to the current page. For example, to apply the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "home"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " layout to the current page, you’d use:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= Home Page\n:page-layout: home"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "See "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page layout"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "page-layout.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to learn about the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-layout"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute and how it can be used to define which UI layout is applied to a page."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Additional predefined page attributes may be added in the future to allow similar kinds of functionality to be configured."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "configure-a-predefined-page-attribute",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Configure a predefined page attribute"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "One of the primary roles of a page attribute is to pass metadata about the page to the UI template via the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "UI model"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "antora-ui-default::templates.html#template-variables"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". The UI template can then use the information provided by the page attributes in a variety of ways, from populating metadata in the published page (i.e, the HTML) to toggling or configuring behavior in the UI."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Let’s look at an example. The default UI allows you do configure the depth of the sidebar TOC using the page attribute named "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "toclevels"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (i.e., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-toclevels"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " when defined)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You could set this attribute globally in your playbook (or component descriptor)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "asciidoc:\n  attributes:\n    page-toclevels: 3@"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The trailing "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is added so the attribute can still can be overridden in the header of a page. For example:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= Page Title\n:page-toclevels: 2"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Page attributes are accessible in the UI model via the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page.attributes"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " property. The value of this property is a map of attributes."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To access the value of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-toclevels"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute in a UI template, you’d use:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "{{page.attributes.toclevels}}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "hbs",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "So where’s the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " prefix gone?"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "When a page attribute is promoted to the UI model, the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " prefix is dropped from its name. That’s why we often refer to the page attribute using its short name (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "toclevels"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " prefix acts as a namespace to identify the attribute as a page attribute. Thus, a page attribute named "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-toclevels"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " becomes "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "toclevels"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in the UI model (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page.attributes.toclevels"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ")."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Let’s look at another example that shows how the default UI uses a page attribute to control pagination. You’ll often set this attribute globally in your playbook or component descriptor. This time, however, we hard set the attribute so it cannot be turned off by a page."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "asciidoc:\n  attributes:\n    page-pagination: ''"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Now, in the footer-scripts.hbs partial template, we can check whether this attribute is set and include the pagination controls if it is."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "{{#unless (eq page.attributes.pagination undefined)}}\n<nav class=\"pagination\">\n...\n</nav>\n{{/unless}}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "hbs",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Notice we check whether the value is not equal to undefined rather than checking if it truthy. That’s because an empty value in JavaScript is falsy, so we have to make the assertion more specific. Inside the clause, the template can check whether the attribute has the value next or prev, implying the opposite direction should be turned off."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " prefix on the attribute name is what hoists it to the UI model. All other document attributes are still accessible from the UI model, just not as easily. Here’s an example of how to reference a non-page attribute from the UI model:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "{{#with (resolvePage page.relativeSrcPath model=false)}}\n{{./asciidoc.attributes.policy-number}}\n{{/with}}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "hbs",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Passing the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page.relativeSrcPath"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " value to the built-in "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "resolvePage"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " helper resolves to the current page. The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "model=false"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " option instructions the helper to return the virtual file rather than the UI model for the resolved page. From there, all the AsciiDoc attributes can be access through the nested "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "asciidoc.attributes"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " property."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "access-attributes-from-ui-template",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Access page attributes from the UI template"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Antora automatically sets a number of read-only, intrinsic page attributes at runtime that are derived from existing metadata about the current page. For example, the name of the current component can be read from the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-component-name"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "These attributes are defined at the time the page or navigation file is loaded (i.e., parsed) They are not yet assigned when the attributes in the component descriptor are resolved, and are thus not visible to the component descriptor."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The intrinsic page attributes are listed on "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "intrinsic-attributes.html"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "intrinsic-attributes.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". These attributes are "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "read-only"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", so you should not override their values in the page header."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "intrinsic-page-attributes",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Intrinsic page attributes"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Page Attributes"
      }
    ]
  }
}
